    {
      "title": "Trump ‘border czar’ says ICE officer in Maine killing should not have cleared vetting",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jul/26/trump-border-czar-ice-officer-maine-killing-vetting",
      "description": "<p>Tom Homan comments on officer’s eligibility to serve after reports that agent’s two ex-wives had accused him of abuse</p><p>Tom Homan, the Trump administration “border czar”, on Sunday said he did not believe the Immigration and Customs Enforcement (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ice-us-immigration-and-customs-enforcement\">ICE</a>) officer at the center of a recent fatal shooting in Maine “should have ever cleared vetting”.</p><p>Speaking to CNN’s State of the Union, Homan was asked by host Dana Bash about the officer’s eligibility to serve following <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fSWB945fv88\">reports</a> that two of his ex-wives had <a href=\"https://www.kcra.com/article/ice-officer-maine-shooting-history-family-records/72902656\">accused</a> him of abuse.</p><p><em>The Associated Press contributed reporting</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jul/26/trump-border-czar-ice-officer-maine-killing-vetting\">Continue reading...</a>",
